{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111967","id":2942020190,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6vW6pe","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111967","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111967.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111967.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111967","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111967/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111967/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111967/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/0f047944e4b34483c8f2b9e529e8ecbd36dbef2d","number":111967,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Statically protect `Object::cast_to` for unrelated `Object` types.","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Introduces static protection to `Object::cast_to`, in the same way that `static_cast` is protected against casting unrelated types together.\r\nThis uncovers a handful of bugs that could have been avoided with this. It will also protect us against new bugs going forwards.\r\n## Bug fixes\r\n\r\nHere's the (necessary) fixes in this PR:\r\n\r\n- `AudioStreamPolyphonic` currently doesn't pass the stream in to stop as expected (passing `nullptr` instead). I changed it to pass the object that was tested for. I'm not sure if my fix is correct, so review required by @godotengine/audio\r\n- `GLTFDocument` attempted to cast `Image` to `Texture2D`, which is impossible. I've removed the casts. If convenience conversion is desired, this should be re-implemented correctly afterwards. cc @aaronfranke \r\n- `SceneImportSettingsDialog::_skeleton_tree_entered` did not set the skin as expected; instead, it currently sets it to `null`. I fixed it in the way that (i think) it was intended.\r\n- The rest of the bugs were inconsequential, since a `nullptr` `Ref` in one type is the same as a `nullptr` ref in another.\r\n- The `PopupMenu::_activate_submenu` change is a really weird one. It casts from `PopupMenu` to `PopupMenu`, and if it doesn't work (which it always does), it returns after calling `popup()`. I think removing this whole logic (which might be leftover after refactors) shouldn't change behavior, because the `if` will never be entered, and `submenu_pum` is equivalent to `submenu_popup`.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repo